 "intro": "Near Munda in southern Spain, March 45 BC. Pompey is dead, but his sons Gnaeus and Sextus have raised thirteen legions. You are Julius Caesar, in the last battle of the civil war. Your old legate Labienus commands their cavalry.",
 "debrief": "In the Spanish War and later accounts, Caesar attacked up a slope and the lines fought for hours without giving way. Caesar himself is said to have gone to the front when his line wavered. The Tenth Legion pushed back the enemy left. When Labienus took cohorts back to stop Bogud’s Moorish horse riding round toward the camp, the Pompeians thought he was retreating, and their line broke. About 30,000 died, Labienus among them. Caesar said he had often fought for victory, but at Munda for his life. The other choices are what-ifs.",
